  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-06T14:16:14.815Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Non-VR Desktop user. Windows 10.\nSince yesterday, I've been witnessing certain problems with my microphone because it simply stopped working suddenly (on VRChat only), and I'm still not sure what could fix it for good, because I got it to work again after many different attempts. However, today, it stopped working yet again.\nBasically, what is going on is that my microphone works everywhere, except in VRChat itself. Yesterday, I installed Equalizer APO and a noise supression dll to improve my microphone's quality. While I'm almost certain the problem started because of this equalizer, I tried not jumping to conclusions and making different attempts to solve the problem, such as:\n-Disabling the \"Allow applications to take exclusive control of this device\" option in the microphone settings.\n-Making triple sure the correct device is selected on VRChat and that I'm not muted.\n-Unplugging the microphone and plugging it in again.\n-Allowing the \"Win32WebViewHost\" application to have access to my microphone after it was randomly deactivated. (Windows key + I > Privacy > Microphone)\n-Restarting both VRChat and my computer itself.\n-Turning off the noise supression (Note: Apparently, the equalizer itself is still on. Not confirmed)",
